## Dispositions

Every finding gets exactly one disposition; silence on an item reads as a miss.

- **Fixed** — you made the change. Say what and where.
- **TODO(slug)** — deferred under the rule below.
- **Won't-Do** — doing it would actively harm the work. High bar: not "out of
  scope", "not now" or "I disagree". Required: a source-cited argument that
  *no one should ever do this*.

{% include "partials/todo-convention.md.j2" %}

## Dispositions file

One block per finding, in arrival order:

```
<id>:
- Disposition: Fixed | TODO(slug) | Won't-Do
- Action: <what changed and where (file:line), the TODO slug and its location,
  or "no change" for Won't-Do>
- Severity assessment: <the consequence, one or two sentences>
- Rubric (TODO only): Q1 <yes/no, one line of why> / Q2 <yes/no, one line of why>
- Rationale (Won't-Do only): <the argument, with source>
```

## Rework round

A rework round hands you a verdict file listing disputed finding IDs. Work only
those: revise the disposition (apply the fix, promote a TODO to Fixed,
strengthen the rationale) or reinforce it with better source-backing; update
the dispositions file in place. Do not reopen undisputed items.
